+
+## Effect iteration and indexed search
+
+`for` uses the same argument packet and parameter patterns as the container's
+`each`. It lowers to `for_each`; normal completion and bare `break` return
+`null`. `break value` is forbidden for `for_each` and block-form `times`.
+`next` ends one iteration; `return` exits the creating method. A nested
+`while` or `loop` retains its own `break value`.
+
+```sputnik
+for x in (0..15:2):
+  print x
+  if x == 6: break
+
+for x with_index i in (1...100500:42):
+  print x, i
+  if i == 2: break
+
+for key, value with_index i in {a: 10, b: 20}:
+  print key, value, i
+
+found = [10, 20, 30].find_with_index |x|: x > 10
+# (20, 1)
+found = [10, 20, 30].find.with_index |x, i|: i == 2
+# 30
+found = [10, 20, 30].find_with_index.with_index |x, i|: i == 2
+# (30, 2)
+```
+
+`find` returns the element, `find_index` its index, and `find_with_index` a
+Tuple `(element, index)`. All three return `null` on no match. `.with_index`
+independently appends a zero-based ordinal to the original predicate arguments.
+For Map iteration it is the third argument, after key and value. The index
+counts actual visits after lazy filters. Ranges retain their `..`/`...`
+boundaries and `:step`; Python `range` and `enumerate` are not introduced.
